      "source_raw_fragment": "<p id=\"A2.SS2.p2.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">The pair <math id=\"A2.SS2.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"(Y_{+},Y_{-})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(Y_{+},Y_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable. We henceforth identify\n<math id=\"A2.SS2.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id=\"A2.SS2.p2.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id=\"A2.SS2.p2.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"f(y)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for a\nmacroscopic observable. Under this identification,</p>"
